url: "https://github.com/ANR-MAMUT/MAMUT-routing-TDVRPTW-Lera2026"
abstract: >-
  Lera2026 is a TDVRPTW benchmark proposed by the listed authors, extending Gehring and Homberger instances to time-dependent routing at 200 to 1000 customers. The construction combines IGP speed profiles with a five-period structure, seeded arc-category assignments and controlled congestion scenarios. Deterministic time-window repair ensures singleton feasibility while retaining the original travel-speed periods. The family is named in honour of Gonzalo Lera-Romero. Its underlying instance data and model components retain the source attributions documented in README.md.
